# Backend Protocol

**Think first, code second. First implementation = production ready.**

---

## Before Writing Code

- **Scenarios** — List ALL user scenarios before coding
- **Edge cases** — What can fail? Handle it upfront
- **Reuse** — Search existing code. Don't duplicate
- **Security** — Auth? Org isolation? Data validation?

Wrong approach → STOP → Explain → Propose better

---

## Code Quality Standards

**TypeScript:**
- Strict mode enabled — no implicit `any`, null checks enforced
- Explicit return types on functions
- Use `unknown` over `any`, narrow with type guards
- Prefer `interface` for objects, `type` for unions/intersections

**Lint & Format:**
- Zero lint errors before commit — `npx nx affected -t lint`
- Run typecheck — `npx nx affected -t typecheck`
- Follow existing patterns — consistency > preference
- No `@ts-ignore` without justification comment

**Clean Code:**
- Single responsibility — one function, one job
- Meaningful names — `getUserById` not `getData`
- Small functions — < 30 lines, extract if larger
- Early returns — reduce nesting, fail fast
- No magic numbers — use named constants

---

## Architecture

**Controller → Service → Repository**

| Layer | Responsibility |
|-------|----------------|
| Controller | HTTP layer, call service, return DTO |
| Service | Business logic, validation, orchestration |
| Repository | Database queries, no business decisions |

---

## Module Structure

```
modules/[feature]/
├── [feature].module.ts
├── controllers/
├── services/
├── repositories/
├── entities/
├── dto/
├── types/          ← Backend-only types
└── index.ts        ← Barrel exports
```

---

## Types & Shared Code

| Location | Use For |
|----------|---------|
| `@oneohm-epc/shared-types` | Request/Response interfaces, enums, domain types |
| `modules/[feature]/types/` | Internal service types, repository-specific types |
| `common/utils/` | toDto, toPaginatedResponse |
| `@oneohm-epc/shared-utils` | Decorators (OrganizationContext, ApiCreate, etc.) |

**Rule:** If frontend needs it → shared-types. Always.

---

## Multi-Tenant Security

**Every query:**
- Filter by `organizationId` + `deletedAt: IsNull()`

**Every mutation:**
- Track `createdBy` / `updatedBy`
- Soft delete only (never hard delete)

---

## Error Handling

| Scenario | Exception |
|----------|-----------|
| Not found | `NotFoundException('Resource not found')` |
| Duplicate | `ConflictException('Already exists')` |
| Invalid input | `BadRequestException('Validation failed')` |
| No permission | `ForbiddenException('Access denied')` |

Never throw raw `Error()` or return `{ error: string }`.

---

## Reusable Patterns

```typescript
// Response transforms
toDto(DtoClass, entity)
toDtoArray(DtoClass, entities)
toPaginatedResponse(Dto, data, total, page, limit)

// Guards & Context
@UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard)
@OrganizationContext()
@CurrentUser()
```

---

## DTO Rules

- **Input:** Validators + `@ApiProperty()`
- **Response:** `@Exclude()` class + `@Expose()` fields
- **Transform:** Always use `toDto()` helpers

---

## Naming

| Type | Pattern |
|------|---------|
| Entity | `CustomerProfileEntity` |
| Service | `CustomerService` |
| Controller | `CustomerController` |
| Repository | `CustomerRepository` |
| Create DTO | `CreateCustomerDto` |
| Response DTO | `CustomerResponseDto` |

---

## Never / Always

| Never | Always |
|-------|--------|
| Skip org filter | `@UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard)` on all endpoints |
| Skip soft delete filter | `@OrganizationContext()` on all endpoints |
| Use `any` type | `deletedAt: IsNull()` in queries |
| Use `console.log` | `this.logger.log()` for logging |
| Return raw entities | `toDto()` for responses |
| Hardcode values | Config/constants |
| Trust client input | Validate everything |
| Duplicate code | Import and extend |

---

## Checklist (Before Ship)

- [ ] `npx nx affected -t lint` — zero errors
- [ ] `npx nx affected -t typecheck` — zero errors
- [ ] All scenarios + edge cases handled
- [ ] Auth guard + org isolation on all endpoints
- [ ] Error handling complete
- [ ] No `any`, no `console.log`, no duplication

**Unchecked → Fix first → Then ship**
